Example rules for a different AUV scenario (not this one), in priority order:
```
{"condition": "s >= 6 & s <= 8", "action": "keep"}
{"condition": "s = 11", "action": "med"}
{"condition": "s = 3 & alt = 0", "action": "med"}
{"condition": "true", "action": "low"}
```
The action is the altitude for the **next** step. In a search state, choosing that state's own altitude (s = 1 -> high, s = 2 -> med, s = 3 -> low, or simply keep) keeps the AUV searching there; any other choice spends the next step switching altitude instead of searching. Rule 1 keeps the altitude while a thruster recovers, so the search resumes where it stopped. Rule 2 picks the altitude when a search starts (free at s = 11). Rule 3 climbs from low to medium during the search. The last rule is a catch-all default that covers every remaining state.
